	(text_box "The perch lies across the top of the tree (J201, a\nsocket on its underside). L201: the levitation coil,\nabout 14 turns on each of 3 layers round an 8 mm hole\n(30 uH, 2.6 ohm; B.Cu stays free for the sensor's\nlines). The printed owl clips over it and holds the bias\nmagnet 14 mm above; the bat floats 8.5 mm under it.\nU201, DRV5055A4 (7.5 mV/mT at 3.3 V, ratiometric), at\nthe coil's centre on the underside, reads the bat's\nmagnet; 1k and 10n at its output keep the coil's\nswitching off the long line down the tree. D201 and D202\nlight the bat from above." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 17.7800 140.9700 0) (size 50.8000 21.5900)
